# Action-row button chrome (required)

Any new pressable control that looks like a game action button (dialogs, overlays, popups, menus, confirms) **must** match the main hand action row (Sort / Call / Pass / Swap / Menu):

- Resting: PokerStars gray pill (`--rack-action-face`, `--rack-action-border-rest`, `--rack-action-shadow-rest`)
- Hover: **no** tint / wash / scale — identical to resting
- Press-in: `--rack-action-face-pressed-chrome` + `--rack-action-pressed`, `transition: none`, `transform: none`
- Wire `.btn--pointer-down` restore (see `buttonPointerPress.ts` + part-0124): `:active:not(.btn--pointer-down)` returns to resting chrome

## Do this

1. Prefer existing opt-in classes already used in the app:
   - `btn btn--primary rack-bottom-tile-cell …__action-btn` (wall-game pattern), or
   - `btn … charleston-error-dialog__rack-action` / menu pill patterns that already share the tokens
2. Copy the **full** action-well token set onto the parent (same as `.panel--hand` action wells in part-0123):
   - `--rack-action-face`, `--rack-action-face-pressed`, `--rack-action-face-pressed-chrome`
   - `--rack-action-shadow-rest`, `--rack-action-pressed`
   - `--rack-action-border-rest`, `--rack-action-border-hold`, `--rack-action-border-color`
   - label colors (`--rack-action-label-color` (+ disabled variants))
3. Opt out of global `.btn:hover` / `.btn:active` wash rules (add the new class next to `wall-game-dialog__action-btn` / `charleston-error-dialog__rack-action` / `blank-exchange-overlay__action-btn` exclusions).
4. Add the part-0124 `:active:not(.btn--pointer-down)` resting restore for the new class.

## Do not

- Invent a one-off gradient, flat gray, or neumorphic inset for “dialog buttons”
- Use only `:active` without the pointer-down restore (press chrome will stick after drag-off)
- Forget `--rack-action-shadow-rest` / `--rack-action-border-rest` on the parent (resting raised look breaks)

Reference implementations: wall-game `wall-game-dialog__action-btn`, blank-exchange `blank-exchange-overlay__action-btn`, menu pills in part-0124.
